{"id":"fa2f50f3fc227c3a45bec4a59ca8ebe9acabe98e","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"fa2f50f3fc227c3a45bec4a59ca8ebe9acabe98e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/features/ec_cpu_connector.md","lines":["@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ vllm serve <model> --ec-transfer-config '{"," ","    The two halves are published together or not at all. An `mm_hash` the producer cannot serve — never saved because the region was full, or evicted since — is reported with empty `metadata` and no address, so an orchestrator leaves the media on the request and the consumer encodes it locally."," 2. The orchestrator issues a follow-up request with the same `mm_hash` to a consumer instance, passing the producer's `ec_transfer_params` through `SamplingParams.extra_args[\"ec_transfer_params\"]`.","-3. On the consumer, `ECCPUScheduler.ensure_cache_available()` reads `request.ec_transfer_params`. For each `mm_hash` not already cached locally, it opens a ZMQ session to `(peer_host, peer_port)`, sends an `XferReq`, and on an `OK` `XferAck` issues a NIXL READ that pulls the blocks straight from the producer's mmap into its own. The request is deferred until the READ completes.","+3. On the consumer, `ECCPUScheduler.ensure_cache_available()` checks `request.ec_transfer_params`. A ready CPU-tier entry or a runner encoder-cache entry with a matching embedding count avoids a remote transfer. For each announced `mm_hash` without either cache hit, it opens a ZMQ session to `(peer_host, peer_port)`, sends an `XferReq`, and on an `OK` `XferAck` issues a NIXL READ that pulls the blocks straight from the producer's mmap into its own. The request is deferred until the READ completes."," 4. A `NACK_NOT_READY` means the producer announced the encoding but its GPU→mmap save has not landed yet. The consumer releases the in-flight entry without recording a failure and re-requests the read on a later step, so a save that lands a few steps late costs latency rather than a recompute."," 5. On any other NACK (`NACK_MISSING`, `NACK_INCOMPAT`, `NACK_VERSION`, `NACK_INTERNAL`), ack timeout, read timeout, or peer disconnect, the consumer discards the in-flight entry and falls back to local encoding for that `mm_hash` — a P2P failure never blocks the request indefinitely."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/v1/core/test_scheduler.py","lines":["@@ -8206,6 +8206,117 @@ def test_ec_connector_ensure_cache_available_defers_request(use_kv_connector):","     _assert_right_encoder_inputs(output, expected_total_reqs=0)"," "," ","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"running\", [False, True])","+def test_ec_connector_does_not_pin_future_runner_hits_at_admission(running):","+    \"\"\"Future hits remain evictable so they cannot block earlier inputs.\"\"\"","+    scheduler = create_scheduler(","+        model=\"llava-hf/llava-1.5-7b-hf\",","+        max_num_batched_tokens=32,","+        use_ec_connector=True,","+        ec_role=\"ec_consumer\",","+    )","+    (request,) = create_requests(","+        num_requests=1,","+        num_tokens=128,","+        mm_positions=[[PlaceholderRange(offset=80, length=32)]],","+    )","+    scheduler.add_request(request)","+    if running:","+        output = scheduler.schedule()","+        assert output.num_scheduled_tokens[request.request_id] == 32","+","+    manager = scheduler.encoder_cache_manager","+    manager.allocate(request, 0)","+    manager.free(request)","+    request.mm_features[0].data = None","+    mm_hash = request.mm_features[0].identifier","+","+    output = scheduler.schedule()","+    assert output.num_scheduled_tokens[request.request_id] == 32","+    assert not output.scheduled_encoder_inputs","+    assert request.request_id not in manager.cached[mm_hash]","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"connector_name\", [\"ECExampleConnector\", \"ECTieringConnector\"])","+def test_ec_connector_schedules_evicted_local_runner_hit(connector_name, tmp_path):","+    \"\"\"A local input can be re-encoded when its runner hit is evicted.\"\"\"","+    ec_config = ECTransferConfig(","+        ec_connector=connector_name,","+        ec_role=\"ec_both\",","+        ec_connector_extra_config={","+            \"ec_cpu_bytes\": 1 << 20,","+            \"shared_storage_path\": str(tmp_path),","+        },","+    )","+    ec_config.mm_encoder_output_widths = {\"image\": 4096}","+    scheduler = create_scheduler(","+        model=\"llava-hf/llava-1.5-7b-hf\",","+        max_num_batched_tokens=64,","+        use_ec_connector=ec_config,","+    )","+    (request,) = create_requests(","+        num_requests=1,","+        num_tokens=128,","+        mm_hashes_list=[[\"new-image\", \"cached-image\"]],","+        mm_positions=[","+            [","+                PlaceholderRange(offset=0, length=32),","+                PlaceholderRange(offset=32, length=32),","+            ]","+        ],","+    )","+    (other,) = create_requests(","+        num_requests=1,","+        mm_hashes_list=[[\"other-image\"]],","+        mm_positions=[[PlaceholderRange(offset=0, length=32)]],","+        req_ids=[\"other\"],","+    )","+    manager = EncoderCacheManager(cache_size=64)","+    scheduler.encoder_cache_manager = manager","+    connector = scheduler.get_ec_connector()","+    assert connector is not None","+    connector.bind_encoder_cache_query(manager.get_cached_num_encoder_embeds)","+    manager.allocate(request, 1)","+    manager.free(request)","+    manager.allocate(other, 0)","+    manager.free(other)","+    request.ec_transfer_params = {\"new-image\": {}}","+    scheduler.add_request(request)","+","+    try:","+        output = scheduler.schedule()","+        assert output.num_scheduled_tokens[request.request_id] == 64","+        assert output.scheduled_encoder_inputs[request.request_id] == [0, 1]","+    finally:","+        scheduler.shutdown()","+","+","+def test_prefill_schedules_placeholder_tokens_without_encoder_embeddings():","+    scheduler = create_scheduler(","+        model=\"llava-hf/llava-1.5-7b-hf\",","+   